  "gotchas": [
    "Auth: one token server for both environments — the docs' Multi-Environment Integrations example sends either environment's credentials to https://idp.flutterwave.com/realms/flutterwave/protocol/openid-connect/token, and Authentication says \"This process applies to both the sandbox and production environments. Make sure to use the correct credentials for each environment to obtain a valid token.\" \"Each token is valid for **10 minutes**\"; \"We recommend refreshing the token at least one minute before it expires.\" Cache the token. Sandbox: \"We archive your test data after 30 days.\"",
    "Headers: send X-Idempotency-Key on this POST. Docs (Idempotency): \"For all `POST` endpoints, include an idempotency key in the request header (`X-Idempotency-Key`).\" The API reference marks it optional; the headers guide lists it under 'Mandatory API Headers'. A reused key replays the first response (\"the response will include the header `X-Idempotency-Cache-Hit: true`\"), so reuse the key when retrying the same operation and use a new one for a new operation. X-Trace-Id is optional. For both: \"It must be a string using only alphanumeric ASCII characters.\" \"Its length should be between 12 and 255 characters.\" The idempotency page also says \"We recommend using a **UUID** string as your idempotency key\": strip the UUID's hyphens to satisfy both.",
    "The body is a union on type: card | mobile_money | ussd | opay | bank_account | applepay | googlepay. Send the matching sibling object (card {…}, mobile_money {country_code, network, phone_number}, ussd {account_bank}). opay and bank_account carry no fields.",
    "card requires only nonce + encrypted_card_number + encrypted_expiry_month + encrypted_expiry_year (encrypted_cvv optional). billing_address and cof are optional; Docs (Card Payments): \"This feature is available only by request.\" (cof, Credential-on-File).",
    "Card encryption: Docs (Encryption): \"When making a card charge request, you **must encrypt** the card information before sending the request.\" \"Retrieve your encryption key from the **API settings** section in your Flutterwave dashboard.\" The documented Node sample encrypts each field with AES-GCM (\"name: \"AES-GCM\"\"): key = the base64-decoded encryption key, IV = the UTF-8 bytes of the nonce (\"Nonce must be exactly 12 characters long\"), output = base64 of the ciphertext. Send the same nonce in the request (card.nonce / pin.nonce). Bad encryption: \"we'll return a `422` error with a failed encryption error message.\" The page's sample error has code 11100, the error table lists 1137400 (a 400): branch on error.type CLIENT_ENCRYPTION_ERROR. FLUTTERWAVE_ENCRYPTION_KEY is an afrotools env-var name; the docs name none. Official backend SDKs encrypt for you.",
    "mobile_money: country_code is the phone dialling code (e.g. \"233\" for Ghana), network the operator (e.g. \"MTN\"), phone_number without the country code.",
    "Method/currency limits: \"USSD payments are only available for NGN (Nigerian Naira) collections.\" OPay: \"This payment method is only available for **NGN** (Nigerian Naira) transactions.\" Pay with Bank (bank_account): \"This payment method is only available for NGN (Nigerian Naira) collections.\" Mobile money: \"The charge `currency` must match the `currency_code` used when creating the payment method.\" The error table gives 1125400 CURRENCY_NOT_SUPPORTED for a mismatch; the mobile money guide's sample returns 10400 REQUEST_NOT_VALID (\"Currency not supported for GH Mobile Money.\").",
    "Store data.id (pmd_…) for create_charge. For recurring card charges, \"set the `recurring` flag to `true` in your charge request\" with the stored payment_method_id. \"Some methods, like USSD and bank transfers, can be reused across customers.\"",
    "Errors: {\"status\":\"failed\",\"error\":{\"type\",\"code\",\"message\",\"validation_errors\"}}; error.code is a string and 400s carry validation_errors[{field_name,message}]. Besides the generic codes (10400 REQUEST_NOT_VALID, 10401, 10403 FORBIDDEN, 10404 RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND, 10409 RESOURCE_CONFLICT, 10422 UNPROCESSABLE, 10500) the error table documents these for this endpoint: 1104400 CARD_NOT_TOKENIZED, 1106400 PAYMENT_METHOD_TYPE_MISSING, 1108400 CARD_RETOKENIZATION_REQUIRED, 1118400 INVALID_CARD_NUMBER, 1135422 CARD_EXPIRY_YEAR_OUT_OF_RANGE, 1136422 CARD_EXPIRY_MONTH_OUT_OF_RANGE, 1142400 USSD_BANK_CODE_INVALID, 1126400 MOBILE_MONEY_COUNTRY_CODE_NOT_SUPPORTED, 1127400 MOBILE_MONEY_NETWORK_NOT_SUPPORTED, 1128500 PAYMENT_CARD_TOKENIZATION_FAILED, 1134422 CARD_EXPIRED, 1137400 CLIENT_ENCRYPTION_ERROR. Branch on error.type / error.code, not on the HTTP status alone. Docs (Errors): \"The current limit is 500 API requests per minute.\" A 429 can come back as a non-JSON page (\"HTML error pages such as `Cloudflare 1015 responses`\"): parse error bodies defensively and back off exponentially with jitter."
  ],
